  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Monday)\nIssued at 1103 AM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nThe aforementioned upper low will navigate eastward along the Red\nRiver on Tuesday. This may lead to a few light showers across SE \nOK Tuesday morning-afternoon, but any meaningful rains are likely \nto remain south of the FA. Moist south/southwest flow will \ncontinue to encourage warmer temperatures Tuesday, with highs in \nthe mid 70s for most. By early in the day Wednesday, a quick- \nmoving shortwave will descend across the C plains, then pivot \nthrough the Midwestern states. This will drag a cold front through\nthe forecast area during the day, likely complicating the \ntemperature forecast. Given the timing of the front, currently \nexpect cooler high temps along and north of I-40 on Wednesday, \nwith warm and moist conditions initially expected across SE OK. If\nthe front does not push through the area until late day, \nlocations along the Red River may see temperatures approaching 80 \ndegrees. Precipitation associated with this system is expected to \nremain east of the CWA.\n\nAnother shortwave and associated cold front are likely to push \nthrough the region Thursday as E CONUS troughing deepens. This will \nensure cooler and drier conditions, along with breezy north winds, \nThursday and Friday. By late Saturday or Sunday, high pressure will \nbegin to move east with southerly flow returning, encouraging \nmoderating temperatures. Low rain chances may eventually return \nto the forecast by early next week as an upper level wave \napproaches from the west.",
